ngest magic.' The dragon bowed and let them pass.\n\nTo reach the Sword of Kings, they had to descend into the Dark Lord Malachar's domain: a fortress of black glass where the sun never shone. the wizard Old Fenwick picked the locks; Rowan Ember carried the light — a single coal of hope in the dark."}, {'n': 4, 'title': 'The Price', 'text': "Rowan Ember did not hesitate. They laid the Sword of Kings on the wizard Old Fenwick's chest, and the light went into the wound, and the wound closed — and the Sword of Kings went dark and cold. The quest's great weapon, spent on one life.\n\nThey marched on the Dark Lord Malachar's stronghold with the Sword of Kings dark but their hearts lit. Rowan Ember carried it anyway, empty as it was. Symbols, the wizard Old Fenwick said, have their own magic.\n\nThen the freed prisoners arrived — an army of the grateful, farmers with pitchforks and smiths with hammers, all come to stand with the bearer of the Sword of Kings. Rowan Ember understood at last: the promise was never the crystal. It was this."}, {'n': 5, 'title': 'The Breaking of the Dark', 'text': "The battle for the kingdom of Eldoria raged from dawn to dusk. the Dark Lord Malachar rode out in black armor, terrible and splendid, and challenged Rowan Ember single combat. The armies held their breath.\n\nThe army of the dark broke and ran. the kingdom of Eldoria was free. Rowan Ember stood in the sudden silence holding the Sword of Kings, which was only a crystal again — but a crystal that had kept its promise.\n\nthe Sword of Kings, dark and cold so long, blazed sudden white — fed not by magic but by the choice. The light struck the Dark Lord Malachar's armor and the armor was empty; the dark lord was only a frightened soul inside, and the soul, seen, fled."}, {'n': 6, 'title': 'The Return', 'text': "They came home to the kingdom of Eldoria in spring, when the orchards bloomed. The songs had already arrived ahead of them, as songs do, and every verse was wrong in the details and right in the heart.\n\nthe wizard Old Fenwick was given the highest honor of the kingdom of Eldoria and immediately used it to demand better roads. Rowan Ember was offered a throne and laughed until they cried. 'I mend fences,' Rowan Ember said.\n\nRowan Ember and the wizard Old Fenwick grew old telling the tale, arguing over every detail, and the kingdom of Eldoria prospered. The prophecy, the elders admitted, had never named a chosen one at all. It had named a choice."}]}

